  sumEn="In 1965 a Welsh-speaking village in the hills above Bala was drowned to give Liverpool water, though thirty-five of the thirty-six members of Parliament for Wales had opposed it and not one voted for it. The story of Capel Celyn, the people who fought for it, and the nation it woke.",
